    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The system uses a <strong>model-free deep reinforcement learning</strong> algorithm to train a neural network policy. The policy maps input states, including the car's velocity, acceleration, and distance measurements, to control commands, such as steering angle and throttle/brake signals. The <strong>reward function</strong> is designed to encourage the agent to maximize the course progress and minimize wall contact.",
